  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef dl_depthwise_separable_convolution(image: list, depthwise_w: list, pointwise_w: list, bias: list = None) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Depthwise Separable Convolution** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef dl_depthwise_separable_convolution(image: list, depthwise_w: list, pointwise_w: list, bias: list = None) -> list:\n    img, dw, pw = np.array(image, dtype=np.float64), np.array(depthwise_w, dtype=np.float64), np.array(pointwise_w, dtype=np.float64)\n    Cin, H, W = img.shape; K = dw.shape[1]; Cout = pw.shape[0]; oh, ow = H - K + 1, W - K + 1\n    dw_o = np.array([[[np.sum(img[c, i:i+K, j:j+K]*dw[c]) for j in range(ow)] for i in range(oh)] for c in range(Cin)])\n    pw_o = np.zeros((Cout, oh, ow))\n    for oc in range(Cout):\n        for ic in range(Cin): pw_o[oc] += pw[oc, ic] * dw_o[ic]\n        if bias: pw_o[oc] += float(bias[oc])\n    return np.round(pw_o, 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
